                                                "sense_id": "48a14fe7-11f6-3c75-9de5-5577fb142b2d",
                                                "text": "In early life our subject was an attendant of Public School No. 17 in Brooklyn, and after fitting himself for business he engaged in various occupations in New York city up to the year 1889, at which time he removed to the town of Hempstead, and during the succeeding six years followed fanning as an occupation."
                                            }
                                        ]
